# CAR at CRVAL2 = 30 with LONPOLE = 180 (synthetic). There is no native pole
# latitude that puts the reference point at native (0, 0) with phi_p = 180
# (wcslib celset: both solutions |latp| > 90), so the header is invalid;
# the old code silently used delta_p = 120. With delta_0 >= theta_0
# wcslib's default would be 0; an explicit 180 must be rejected, not replaced.
# EXPECT-WCSLIB-ERROR: No valid solution for latp
NOTE reject: lonpole_car_dec30_lp180
GRID 1 512 9 1 512 9
PIX 256.5 256.5
SKYGRID 90 110 5 15 45 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'RA---CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--CAR'
CRVAL1  = 100.0
CRVAL2  = 30.0
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.1
CDELT2  = 0.1
LONPOLE = 180.0
